# init-audit.py --check allowlist: resident functions permitted to reference
# discardable sections (INIT / INITDATA / .rsrc).
#
# An entry asserts: EVERY path through this function that dereferences a
# discardable address completes before Phase1Initialization runs
# MiFindInitializationCode/MiFreeInitializationCode.  Names are compared
# after stripping stdcall/fastcall decoration and LTO clone suffixes
# (.lto_priv/.constprop/.isra/.part/.cold).
#
# Adding an entry requires the same review bar as an INIT migration:
# explain WHY the reference cannot execute post-discard.  "the suite
# passed" is not a justification.

# The Phase-1 orchestrator itself: calls Phase1InitializationDiscard and
# the MiFindInitializationCode/MiFreeInitializationCode pair.  Runs in
# .text precisely so it survives the discard it performs; everything INIT
# it touches happens before (or is) the free.
Phase1Initialization

# The boot PnP dispatch chain (ClassDispatchPnp, PciIdeXDispatchPnp,
# AtaDispatchPnp, PartMgrPnp, PciPnpControl, PdoDispatchPnp, the
# AddDevice/START handlers under them) moved INTO INIT 2026-06-10 --
# their former resident->INIT references are INIT->INIT now, and
# IopSealBootDriverPnp stamps the driver objects' PnP entry points back
# to IopInvalidDeviceRequest before the discard.  PciIdeXInitialize
# stays: pciide's DriverEntry-time miniport registration calls
# IoAllocateDriverObjectExtension (INIT) and remains resident (it is an
# exported-shape helper, standalone on DBG builds).
PciIdeXInitialize

# KdInitSystem's INIT targets are first-call-only: the
# KdRegisterDebuggerDataBlock call is guarded by the data-list head not
# yet existing, and the KdDebuggerInitialize0 call needs EnableKd, which
# a re-entry only sets when KD was never enabled at boot.  Our DBG flash
# bakes /DEBUG into LoadOptions, so KD enables at boot and bugcheck-time
# re-entry returns at the KdDebuggerEnabled early-out.  CAVEAT: a DBG
# kernel booted WITHOUT /DEBUG that bugchecks post-boot would reach the
# discarded KdDebuggerInitialize0 -- that configuration does not exist
# in our boot chain.
KdInitSystem

# MmZeroPageThread's MiFindInitializationCode call is skipped via the
# NxInitFreesDone latch, set by Phase1Initialization before the discard
# (see xb/mm/init.c).
MmZeroPageThread

# PspCreateProcess calls MmInitializeHandBuiltProcess(2) only on the
# Parent == NULL path -- the hand-built System process during Phase 1.
# Titles cannot create processes (single-process model, no such
# ordinal), so the path never runs post-discard.
PspCreateProcess

